(footprint "RPi_PicoW_SMD_TH"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Raspberry Pi Pico W / Pico 2 W dual-mount carrier footprint for amigahid-pico rev6: all 40 edge pads are BOTH plated through-holes on the 2x20 2.54 mm grid (x=+-8.89) AND elongated castellation pads (x=+-9.69, 3.2x1.6, overhanging the module edge at +-10.5) - socket the module on 2x20 female headers for proto, or solder it flat by its castellations for final builds. USB test points TP2 (USB_DM) / TP3 (USB_DP) at the module's stock coordinates (+-1.0, -24.3) but built as rev5's proven USB tap: 1.6 mm pads on 1.3 mm drills bisected by a 2.0 x 3.81 mm Edge.Cuts slot, giving two castellated half-vias you can solder to the module's underside test pads once it is mounted flat (the tap is non-functional when the module is socketed for proto - use a micro-USB OTG dongle then). Expect a copper-to-edge DRC exception on those two pads: that is what a castellation is. TP1/TP4/TP5/TP6 are deliberately ABSENT - the carrier has no net for them and netless copper trapped under a flat-soldered module cannot be reworked. 3-pin mid-board debug port as through-holes 41/42/43 (SWCLK/GND/SWDIO), 4 USB shell ground pads (SH), 2.4 GHz antenna + RF copper keep-out zones retained from the official land pattern. Edge/castellation/test-point/keep-out geometry from https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/picow/pico-w-datasheet.pdf (via KiCad 10 Module:RaspberryPi_Pico_W_SMD); through-hole grid from KiCad 10 Module:RaspberryPi_Pico_Common_Unspecified. Reflow paste apertures deleted - the module is hand-soldered or socketed.")
	(tags "module raspberry pi pico picow pico2w usb pcb swd antenna castellated tht smd dual-mount amigahid rev6")
